R CMD INSTALL: compile preflight (rzig's check mode names what is missing)

A package needs the toolchain when it has compiled code (src/) or a
configure script R runs: configure, or on Windows configure.ucrt or
configure.win (there R does not run a plain configure, it only warns).
rzig, R_HOME/bin/toolchain/zig-cc (gcc.exe on Windows), finds each
toolchain group's tools as a compile does, on every channel: its check
mode `--rzig-check=package` (check.zig) decides for the package in the
working directory, as `rzig build` (patch 0013, feat-zig-pkg-build)
decides in run_shlib, through one function (pkgbuild.decide: the
files, then the Makevars and Makeconf), whether it builds through zig
build alone (tiers 0-2) or needs make (tier 3), and checks the groups
that build needs: the compilers, flang when Fortran is compiled (the
plan's sources for tiers 1 and 2; src/'s top level, either case of the
f, for a package make builds, as R's default OBJECTS rule compiles
them: Fortran a Makevars builds from a subdirectory stops later, at
zig-fc, with the same text), and the build tools when the package needs
make or R runs a configure script (R_ZIG_CONFIGURE=1), whatever its
tier. A check that fails exits non-zero after a line saying what is
missing, with rzig's own reason when make is needed ("<pkg> needs make:
src/Makevars has a rule or target line: '...'; no make on PATH"), and
the group's text, which names how to install it. Run it before the
configure step and stop with that text, instead of failing deep in
configure or make. With no rzig at all (R without its toolchain
package), stop with one message naming the package to install, from
R_ZIG_TOOLCHAIN_HINT (the conda and wheel builds set it). The C
standard (use_C, the hook's --c-std) goes through R_ZIG_C_STD;
R_ZIG_PKG_BUILDER=make makes the check ask for the build tools. A user
Makevars (their own compiler) or R_ZIG_NO_PREFLIGHT skips the check;
binary packages never reach it. Two inputs differ from the hook's, and
are recorded: CLINK_CPPFLAGS is set only after the preflight, and the
user-Makevars skip stays.
feat-no-host-paths PLAN.md, phase T; feat-standalone-toolchain PLAN.md,
B26 and B35; feat-zig-pkg-build PLAN.md, consolidation M1.

