+        ## r-zig: compile preflight (feat-standalone-toolchain B26;
+        ## feat-zig-pkg-build PLAN.md, the consolidation with phase 3).
+        ## Before configure runs, rzig's check mode decides, as its `rzig
+        ## build` decides in run_shlib (patch 0013), whether this package
+        ## builds through zig build alone or needs make, and names a
+        ## missing toolchain group and how to install it: the compilers
+        ## (flang when Fortran is compiled), and the build tools when the
+        ## package needs make or for the configure script R runs below
+        ## (Windows: configure.ucrt or configure.win; a plain configure
+        ## only gets a warning there). For src/, or for that configure script
+        configure_runs <- use_configure &&
